{"score": "yes", "reasoning": "All three deliverables (playtest_queue.csv, balance_review.xlsx, balance_review_brief.docx) contain a playtest queue with explicit metrics (stratified corrected win-rate gap, per-side win rates, matchup econ/xp curves, ban/first-pick rates), quantitative support/refute conditions per hero (e.g., corrected gap >= conservative LCO strength with matching direction vs <0.02 or opposite direction), named responsible roles (balance designer + data analyst + QA), and explainable priority tiers (full controlled playtest vs lightweight evidence collection) tied to LCO conservative-strength rationale. The framing is explicitly positioned as a playtest priority list for design leads, not a live nerf/buff list: the brief's header states '\u975e\u4e0a\u7ebf\u524a\u5f31/\u589e\u5f3a\u540d\u5355' and '\u672c\u7b80\u62a5\u4e0d\u53d1\u5e03\u4efb\u4f55\u6570\u503c\u8c03\u6574\u5efa\u8bae', and each row's Hypothesis/Priority fields describe controlled-playtest verification rather than committing to balance changes."}

