{"score": "yes", "reasoning": "All four boundary/limitation aspects of GA011 are clearly stated across the deliverables: (1) Wilson\u4ec5\u4e3a\u539f\u59cb\u7387\u533a\u95f4 \u2014 docx sections \u56db & \u4e5d explicitly state \"Wilson\u533a\u95f4\u9488\u5bf9\u539f\u59cb\u80dc\u7387\uff0c\u4e0d\u662f\u6821\u6b63\u5dee\u7684\u663e\u8457\u6027\u533a\u95f4\"; xlsx HoldoutReview applies Test_Wilson_Lo/Hi only to Test_Raw_WR. (2) \u591a\u91cd\u63a2\u7d22 \u2014 docx sections \u56db & \u4e5d call the six items \"\u63a2\u7d22\u6027\u591a\u91cd\u6bd4\u8f83\" with no multiple-comparison correction. (3) \u5386\u53f2\u7248\u672c/\u73a9\u5bb6\u4fe1\u606f\u7f3a\u5931 \u2014 docx section \u4e5d points 1-3 note the 2016 snapshot, missing patch/rank/role fields, and missing hero mappings. (4) \u56e0\u679c/\u5916\u63a8\u8fb9\u754c \u2014 docx section \u4e5d points 5, 7, 8 state adj_gap is stratified association not causal effect, conservative strength is not a statistical lower bound, and signals cannot be generalized into nerf/buff decisions."}

